{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["R59", "D14"],
      "pins": ["R59.2", "D14.4", "D14.2"],
      "nets": ["NET0188", "Net-(D14-K2)"],
      "observed": "R59 pin 2 is connected to NET0188, the same net as D14 pin 4 (A2). D14 pin 2 (K2) connects only to R59 pin 1, forming a closed loop with no path to ground.",
      "expected": "R59 should be a current-limiting resistor from D14 K2 to GND, so that when NET0188 is high, current flows through D14 A2-K2 and R59 to ground, lighting the LED.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"133\") (name \"NET0188\") ... (node (ref \"R59\") (pin \"2\") ...))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"161\") (name \"Net-(D14-K2)\") ... (node (ref \"D14\") (pin \"2\") ...) (node (ref \"R59\") (pin \"1\") ...))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"133\") (name \"NET0188\") ... (node (ref \"D14\") (pin \"4\") ...))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The second LED of dual LED D14 will never illuminate because its cathode resistor returns to the same signal net instead of ground, so the e-stop/status indication on NET0188 is lost.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U8", "U48"],
      "pins": ["U8.4", "U8.5", "U48.4", "U48.5"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "Both GND1 (pin 4) and GND2 (pin 5) of the isolated CAN transceivers U8 and U48 are tied to the same GND net. VCC2 is also supplied from the non-isolated 5V_switched_CAN rail.",
      "expected": "For isolated CAN buses, GND2 and VCC2 should be on an isolated ground/power domain separate from the logic-side GND1/VCC1, preserving galvanic isolation.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"53\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"4\") ...) (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"5\") ...) (node (ref \"U48\") (pin \"4\") ...) (node (ref \"U48\") (pin \"5\") ...))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller ... through an isolated CAN transceiver"}
      ],
      "impact": "The CAN interfaces are not galvanically isolated; ground loops and common-mode voltages between the rover and motor controllers can couple into the logic side, defeating the intended isolation.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain at least two anomalies: R59 is miswired so one channel of dual LED D14 cannot light, and the isolated CAN transceivers have their isolated and logic grounds tied together, defeating the specified isolation."
}

